OL,3,GNEWSACrash survivor speaks out on day
OL,4,Aof remembrance
OL,5,
OL,6,FMemorial services have been held across
OL,7,Fthe West Midlands to remember those who
OL,8,Fhave been killed or seriously injured
OL,9,Fin road collisions.
OL,11,FAmong those speaking were David
OL,12,FJenkins, who spent three months in a
OL,13,Fcoma after a crash in 2022 and the
OL,14,FWarwickshire Police and Crime
OL,15,FCommissioner Philip Seccombe, who lost
OL,16,Fa young member of his family in a
OL,17,Fcrash.
OL,19,FSeccombe said he wanted to educate
OL,20,Fdrivers, especially young ones, about
OL,21,Fthe dangers of the road.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,354,350,200,160,0,100
